  ],
  "_ordering_note": "Learn is an ORDERED LADDER cut into its natural STAGES: Where You Are, Grow Food, Water, Shelter and Power, When Somebody Is Hurt, Making and Repair. Reading them in order, and the documents within each in order, walks the ladder rung for rung. A new guide goes at its RUNG, not on the end of whatever category looks closest. An earlier note proposed splitting Learn into the syllabus's 18 subjects once curriculum landed. That was reconsidered on 2026-09-15 and rejected: subject shelves of one or two documents destroy the order a beginner walks, and the subject view already exists in the Library's Curriculum face, which renders data/curriculum/syllabus.json directly. Cutting at the STAGES costs nothing, because the reading order across them is unchanged. It was done when Real Skills reached 21 documents and became the long scroll that sections were introduced to fix."
}
